                <pb facs="1039" n="925" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg925"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.252/64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-28T17:00:00-04:00">September 28, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>121. Department’s telegram No. 45, September 28, noon. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Modus vivendi</hi> signed this afternoon. The Foreign Office insisted upon
                    15 days’ cancellation clause since agreement with France contains this
                    provision.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
